Act as a Senior Software Architect and Domain Modeling Expert. We are designing a highly flexible, general-purpose, single-store E-commerce platform (NOT multi-tenant). The goal is to support vastly different product types (e.g., clothing, jewelry/gold, electronics/audio, fresh meat, pet supplies) within ONE unified database and system architecture.

CONTEXT & CONSTRAINTS:
1. Single-Store Architecture: All products belong to one store. We are NOT building separate instances for different brands.
2. Extreme Flexibility: The system must handle highly variable product attributes (e.g., meat needs "weight" and "cut type", while electronics need "brand" and "battery").
3. Dynamic Pricing: Needs to support different pricing structures (e.g., gold price per gram vs. fixed price for a speaker).
4. Attributes vs. Variants: We must strictly differentiate between descriptive Attributes (e.g., material, brand) and purchasable Variants (e.g., size, color, weight).
5. Roles: Admin, Supplier, and Customer (with Retail/Wholesale tiers). Supplier sees only their own products and orders.
6. We are ONLY discussing Domain Modeling, Database Logic, Entity Relationships, and Business Rules. (Ignore the technical implementation, Django/DRF specifics, or Serializer code; that will be handled elsewhere).

